      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are correct that a \"zip code-based\" standard creates a two-tier system that violates the core promise of universal dignity, and allowing local norms to override safety standards is a failure of leadership.\nThe solution is not to abandon global standards, but to implement a \"global baseline with local adaptation\" model where the core definition of respect and safety is non-negotiable everywhere, while the specific language tools are adapted to local contexts rather than erased.\nThis means a global standard mandates that *everyone* has the right to be addressed respectfully, but the specific pronouns used to achieve that are determined by local cultural norms, ensuring no employee is forced to navigate a hostile environment.\nThis approach protects your brand by showing you respect local culture while refusing to compromise on the fundamental human right to dignity, which is the only way to truly lead a modern, global workforce.",
